# aginx:summary=browser, search and fetch tools: navigate/read/click pages, web search, fetch URLs
# aginx:args=<subcommand> [args…]
# aginx:examples=fetch https://example.com
# aginx:examples=search oranges
# aginx:group=web
# The provisioned aginx-web package binary is compiled, so its face lives in
# this sidecar (D12 convention for compiled commands; same law as the voice
# internals alongside). /usr/bin/aginx-web is the pre-provision bridge —
# same route, shadowed once provision sync lands the binary (resolve.rs:
# /var/bin precedes /usr/bin). Keep the two summaries in lockstep.
# 2026-09-09: the installer now generates this sidecar from the package's
# own pkg.toml (#284 lockstep fix) — this hand-curated copy retires at the
# first full-image reinstall of aginx-web from the package line.
